1 NAME Mariano Hugo /zu Windisch-Graetz/
2 GIVN Mariano Hugo
2 SURN zu Windisch-Graetz
2 _MARNM zu Windisch-Graetz
1 NAME Mariano Hugo, Prince of Windisch-Graetz
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 JUL 1955
2 PLAC Friuli-Venezia Giulia
2 ADDR
3 CITY Trieste
3 CTRY Italia
1 OCCU Ambassador, Fürst (prince)
1 TITL prince
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * House of Habsburg: Knight of the Austrian Order of the Golden Fleece.
2 CONT * [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:mopkQdYJ8AIJ:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariano_Hugo_of_Windisch-Graetz+&cd=1&hl=en&ct=clnk&lr= en.wikipedia - '''Hugo of Windisch-Graetz''']
2 CONT * Hugo Windisch-Graetz was born in Trieste as the elder son of Maximilian, Prince zu Windisch-Graetz and Maria Luisa (Marlise) Serra di Gerace His mother was the legitimatised daughter of Gian Battista Serra, 12th Principe di Gera
2 CONC ce by Donna Maria Grazia Carafa d'Andria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugo Windisch-Graetz was educated firstly in Rome at the school of the De La Salle Brothers[citation needed] and then in England at the University College of Buckingham,[citation needed] from which he graduated in 1975 with a degr
2 CONC ee in economics and political science.
2 CONT
2 CONT When his father died in 1976, Windisch-Graetz succeeded as head of a cadet branch of the House of Windisch-Graetz, a mediatised house whose members historically bear the style of Serene Highness.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 11 February 1990 in Salzburg, Austria, Windisch-Graetz '''married''' Archduchess Sophie of Austria, daughter of Archduke Ferdinand and Countess Helen zu Toerring-Jettenbach. The Countess was a grand niece of Queen Elisabeth of 
2 CONC the Belgians and daughter of Princess Elizabeth of Greece and Denmark, making her a first cousin of the current Duke of Kent. The couple had three children: Prince Maximilian Hugo, Prince Alexis Ferdinand (who died at Sant'Angelo 
2 CONC d'Alife in a car accident in 2010), and Princess Larissa Maria Grazia Helen Leontina Maria Luisa.Windisch-Graetz and his family reside in Italy when he is not abroad on diplomatic appointment, maintaining a home in Rome and Il Pal
2 CONC azzo in Sant'Angelo d'Alife
